Parallax effect is a website design trend which is achieved using a few CSS properties. In this effect the speed of scrolling of the content is different from the
scrolling speed of Images due to which it gives a sense of stationary background images with text scrolling above the images.
The CSS properties are applied to the images of the page. these are as follows,
    background-attachment: fixed;
    background-position: center;
    background-size: cover;

background-attachment: fixed; fixes the image on the page. The 'background-position' property sets the position of images and 'background-size' determines its 
size or coverage on the page.

The CSS positions is a property which is used to set a position of an element on the page. The commonly used CSS position values are,
> position: static; It does not move the element. The element stays fixed on its position according to the normal flow of HTML. 
The top, right, bottom, left, and z-index properties have no effect. This is the default value.
> position: relative; When its set to an element, the element can be positioned using the top, right, bottom, left, and z-index properties with respect to
its normal position.
> position: absolute; When its set on an element, the element is removed from the normal flow of document and no space is provided for it on the place where it 
should be placed. Now, the position of this element is set in relation to the closest ancestoral element with a CSS position property applied.
